1
00:04:31,304 --> 00:04:37,304
In one small bottle... The fountain of youth. The secret of eternal life. The power
of an ancient potion. Sometimes it works... sometimes it doesn't.

2
00:09:02,608 --> 00:09:08,608
Death Becomes Her is a comedy, fantasy, horror film directed by Robert Zemeckis.

3
00:13:33,913 --> 00:13:39,913
Madeline is married to Ernest, who was once her arch-rival Helen's fiancé.

4
00:18:05,217 --> 00:18:11,217
After recovering from a mental breakdown, Helen vows to
kill Madeline and steal back Ernest.

5
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:42,521
Unfortunately for everyone, the introduction of a magic potion causes things
to be a great deal more complicated than a mere murder plot.

6
00:27:07,826 --> 00:27:13,826
Madeline Ashton Menville, played by Meryl Streep.

7
00:31:39,130 --> 00:31:45,130
Helen Sharp, played by Goldie Hawn.

8
00:36:10,434 --> 00:36:16,434
Dr. Ernest Menville, played by Bruce Willis.

9
00:40:41,739 --> 00:40:47,739
Lisle von Rhuman, played by Isabella Rossellini.

10
00:45:13,043 --> 00:45:19,043
Chagall, played by Ian Ogilvy.

11
00:49:44,347 --> 00:49:50,347
Dakota, played by Adam Storke.

12
00:54:15,652 --> 00:54:21,652
Death Becomes Her is a 1992 American surrealist black comedy fantasy film directed and
produced by Robert Zemeckis and written by David Koepp and Martin Donovan.

13
00:58:46,956 --> 00:58:52,956
The film stars Meryl Streep, Goldie Hawn, Bruce Willis, and Isabella Rossellini.

14
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:24,260
Its plot follows two women who drink a magic potion that promises eternal youth.

15
01:07:49,565 --> 01:07:55,565
Filming began in December 1991 and concluded in April
1992; it was filmed in Los Angeles.

16
01:12:20,869 --> 01:12:26,869
Death Becomes Her was released in the United States by
Universal Pictures on July 31, 1992.

17
01:16:52,173 --> 01:16:58,173
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:21:23,478 --> 01:21:29,478
It was also a pioneer in the use of computer-generated effects and went
on to win the Academy Award for Best Visual Effects.

19
01:25:54,782 --> 01:26:00,782
The film is regarded as a cult classic and a highly
treasured film within the gay community.

20
01:30:26,086 --> 01:30:32,086
It has since been adapted into a critically acclaimed
Tony Award-winning Broadway musical.

21
01:34:57,391 --> 01:35:03,391
The film explores themes of jealousy, immortality, beauty, rivalry, potion.

22
01:39:28,695 --> 01:39:34,695
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
